Build only flex_fidl of fdomain/client, for Fuchsia (milestone M9b).

Pilot 1's closure uses only :flex_fidl (crate flex_client without the fdomain feature;
docs/closure/pilot1.json). :client (crate fdomain_client) needs fuchsia.fdomain's
bindings and //src/lib/fidl/rust/fidl_message, and :flex_fdomain needs :client: outside
the closure, so both targets are removed. On host, :flex_fidl builds with
//src/lib/fuchsia-emulated-handle (outside the closure too): the host branch is emptied
and the target marked Fuchsia-only.

The added lines are the overlay's (Apache-2.0); the context lines are Fuchsia's
(BSD-2-Clause, LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt). Applied by scripts/regen.py to the rewritten
BUILD.bazel.

